Fix: install the codegen tool from a RelWithDebInfo build too (one SDK build, not two)

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk)
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0019-codegen-tool-in-relwithdebinfo.patch
Status:     build-time improvement (could go upstream)

WHAT WAS SLOW
  The game builds in RelWithDebInfo (its runtime libraries are the "rd"
  ones), but the codegen tool `rexglue` was installed ONLY from a Release
  build. A fresh setup therefore built and installed the whole SDK TWICE:
  Release (only for the tool) and RelWithDebInfo (for the game). On player
  PCs that doubled the longest step of the Windows installer.

FIX
  - cmake/rexglue_install.cmake: the tool is installed for Release AND
    RelWithDebInfo (both optimised; RelWithDebInfo's file is rexgluerd(.exe),
    the SDK's usual postfix).
  - cmake/rexglueConfig.cmake.in: consumers map each config to a LIST, the
    first installed one wins (Release first, then RelWithDebInfo), so an
    install with either build works. Release first on purpose: an install
    made before this patch keeps its Release tool, the game's recompile
    command stays the same and nothing is recompiled because of the switch.
  Building only `--config RelWithDebInfo --target install` is then enough.

HOW FOUND
  Reading the installer's SDK step (launcher/setup.cpp SdkJob) while looking
  into very slow Windows installs (2026-11-08).

diff --git a/cmake/rexglueConfig.cmake.in b/cmake/rexglueConfig.cmake.in
index ff7f132..a98de84 100644
--- a/cmake/rexglueConfig.cmake.in
+++ b/cmake/rexglueConfig.cmake.in
@@ -38,12 +38,15 @@ endif()
 
 include("${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/rexglueTargets.cmake")
 
-# Only Release rexglue is installed, so every consumer config has to reach it.
+# Only Release / RelWithDebInfo rexglue is installed, so every consumer config
+# has to reach one of them (the first one installed wins). Release first: an
+# install that has it (built before 0019) keeps running the same tool, so the
+# game's recompile step doesn't see a new command and redo everything.
 if(TARGET rex::rexglue)
     set_target_properties(rex::rexglue PROPERTIES
-        MAP_IMPORTED_CONFIG_DEBUG Release
-        MAP_IMPORTED_CONFIG_RELWITHDEBINFO Release
-        MAP_IMPORTED_CONFIG_MINSIZEREL Release)
+        MAP_IMPORTED_CONFIG_DEBUG "Release;RelWithDebInfo"
+        MAP_IMPORTED_CONFIG_RELWITHDEBINFO "Release;RelWithDebInfo"
+        MAP_IMPORTED_CONFIG_MINSIZEREL "Release;RelWithDebInfo")
 endif()
 
 if(TARGET rex::runtime AND NOT TARGET rex::system)
diff --git a/cmake/rexglue_install.cmake b/cmake/rexglue_install.cmake
index d9a64eb..21ca018 100644
--- a/cmake/rexglue_install.cmake
+++ b/cmake/rexglue_install.cmake
@@ -52,10 +52,13 @@ install(TARGETS ${REXGLUE_INSTALL_TARGETS}
 )
 
 # A Debug codegen tool runs an order of magnitude slower, so only Release ships.
+# RelWithDebInfo too (optimised as well): a consumer that builds only
+# RelWithDebInfo then needs ONE SDK build, not a whole second Release one just
+# for this tool.
 install(TARGETS rexglue
     EXPORT rexglueTargets
     RUNTIME DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_BINDIR}
-    CONFIGURATIONS Release
+    CONFIGURATIONS Release RelWithDebInfo
 )
 
 if(REXGLUE_INSTALL_FIDELITYFX_TARGETS)
